Beryllium: report the GPU process's real sandbox state (RT-17)

Purpose: beryllium://gpu showed "Sandboxed: true" on the owner's
  16.0-CURRENT machine (3 November 2026), as chrome://gpu does for the stock
  FreeBSD Chromium. It is false: the FreeBSD port's
  SandboxLinux::InitializeSandbox() (sandbox/policy/freebsd/sandbox_freebsd.cc,
  from the imported BSD patches) applies no confinement and returns true in
  every case, even with --no-sandbox, and the GPU process reports that value.
  A browser that claims a sandbox it does not have misleads users and
  reviewers.
  On FreeBSD the GPU process now reports sandboxed only if the kernel says
  it is in Capsicum capability mode (cap_getmode(2)). Today that is false;
  once Beryllium's sandbox enters capability mode in the GPU process, the
  report becomes true with no further change.
  The value is only displayed (beryllium://gpu) and recorded in UMA, which
  is disabled; nothing in the browser acts on it (checked in gpu_init.cc,
  gpu_process_host.cc, gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc, gpu_util.cc), and
  "false" is its default on every platform. InitializeSandbox() itself is
  left unchanged because other process types use its result.
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series). Depends on the imported BSD patches
  patch-content_gpu_gpu__main.cc and patch-sandbox_policy_freebsd_*.
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca),
  FreeBSD ports 6ad3e0c8, using freebsd/tools/patch-workbench; the new code
  compiled against FreeBSD 16.0-CURRENT headers.
Test: beryllium://gpu shows "Sandboxed: false" (plan/12 RT-17);
  freebsd/tests (planned) checks it against procstat for the GPU process.
security-review: required (sandbox reporting)

--- a/content/gpu/gpu_main.cc
+++ b/content/gpu/gpu_main.cc
@@ -127,6 +127,10 @@
 #include "sandbox/policy/sandbox_type.h"
 #endif
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_FREEBSD)
+#include <sys/capsicum.h>
+#endif
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 #include "base/message_loop/message_pump_apple.h"
 #include "components/metal_util/device_removal.h"
@@ -582,7 +586,16 @@
     tracing::PerfettoTracedProcess::Get().RestartThreadInSandbox();
   }
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_FREEBSD)
+  // Beryllium (RT-17): the FreeBSD SandboxLinux::InitializeSandbox() applies
+  // no confinement and always returns true, which beryllium://gpu showed as
+  // "Sandboxed: true". Report what the kernel says instead: sandboxed only
+  // if this process is in Capsicum capability mode.
+  u_int cap_mode = 0;
+  return res && cap_getmode(&cap_mode) == 0 && cap_mode != 0;
+#else
   return res;
+#endif
 }
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
 
